# V2-E05 gate transcript — GREEN (M1)

The red→green cycle for the plugin compatibility harness (WP V2-E05).
Recorded under `scripts/gates/` per the house TDD rule. Companion to
`e05_red.log`.

## GREEN — every E05 leg landed + verified V8-free

The V8-free gates that run in this sandbox (the CLI binary does not link
here — ENOSPC on the final `cc` link, the dep tree + binary exceed the 10 GB
disk; the CLI-dependent gates ride CI, listed below).

### Node suite (zero deps, V8-free)

    $ node --test conformance/plugins/test/*.test.mjs
    ℹ tests 24
    ℹ pass 24
    ℹ fail 0

Pins: the case schema (`validateCase` good + 5 bad shapes, every committed
case validates), the assert evaluator (glob `*`/`**`, missing-root no-throw,
contains pass/fail), the report parser (structured `oxide-plugin-load` line +
the `PLG-HOOK` fail-at-load arm + multi-message merge + empty-log), the
matrix renderer (deterministic, pipe-escape, tally).

### The dry-run consumer example (renders the matrix end-to-end)

    $ node scripts/plugin-compat.mjs --dry-run
    wrote conformance/plugins/results.json (10 cases; 9 pass, 0 fail, 1 unsupported-hook)

    $ node scripts/plugin-compat.mjs --dry-run --out -
    | Plugin | Version | Adapter | Status | Unsupported hooks | Asserts | Note |
    | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
    | `@mdx-js/rollup` | `3.1.1` | react | pass | — | 1/1 | — |
    ...
    | `vite-plugin-pwa` | `2.0.0` | react | unsupported-hook | configureServer | 0/1 | declares configureServer (bridge-unsupported; the plugin fails at load so its output never lands) |
    ...

Ten third-party plugins verified (Part I §24.1 item 6). Package + version
verified via `npm view` (7.3.1 / 6.0.11 / 2.11.17 / 3.1.1 / 5.2.0 / 4.3.5 /
24.0.0 / 6.1.1 / 2.0.0 / 6.3.0). Failures documented, not hidden (the §V2-E05
acceptance): `vite-plugin-pwa` declares `configureServer` (bridge-unsupported,
`PLG-HOOK` at load) → `unsupported-hook`.

### The Rust load-time report pins (plugin crate)

    $ cargo test -p oxide-fw-plugin --test compat_tdd
    test result: ok. 25 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored

New pins: `host_invocable_hooks_matches_the_compat_model`,
`unsupported_hooks_names_the_bridge_refused_ones_for_js`,
`unsupported_hooks_folds_both_wasm_gaps`, `unsupported_hooks_is_empty_for_native`,
`load_time_report_partitions_declared_hooks`,
`load_time_report_json_uses_camel_case_hook_names`,
`wasm_load_time_report_records_the_silent_gap`,
`registry_records_a_load_report_per_accepted_plugin`,
`registry_emit_load_reports_jsonl_carries_the_prefix`. The existing
`plugin_compat_doc_embeds_the_generated_table` pin stays GREEN (the kind×hook
table is byte-identical in the regenerated `docs/plugin-compat.md`).

### The config_refusal Live pin fix (adapters crate, ADDITIVE)

    $ cargo test -p oxide-fw-adapters --test config_refusal_tdd
    test result: ok. 17 passed; 0 failed

The V2-E09 drift: `warns_live_on_degraded_cells_with_the_documented_string`
