The existing criterion benches (`crates/plugin/benches/compat.rs`) stay green.

## CI gates (not run in this sandbox — the CLI binary link + the full
## workspace exceed the 10 GB disk; listed with the exact job names)

- `docs-check` — `cargo run -p oxide-fw-cli -- docs --root . generate --check`
  (regenerates `docs/plugin-compat.md` + `docs/reference/*.md`, fails on drift;
  the `PluginCompatPage` generator + the `errors_registry_tdd` /
  `docs_tdd` integration tests).
- `node` — the ten-plugin install+build (real mode) + the pnpm workspace
  suites; refreshes `conformance/plugins/results.json`.
- `rust/test` — `cargo test --workspace --all-features` (the
  `errors_registry_tdd` + `docs_tdd` CLI integration tests + the config_refusal
  pin + the compat_tdd pin).
- `rust/lint` — `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D
  warnings -W pedantic` (the full-workspace pedantic gate — M2's per-crate
  hygiene pass for the eight own-table crates).
- `conformance` — the §22 cross-adapter assertion registry.
- `bench-gate` — the criterion benches.

`docs/plugin-compat.md` + `docs/reference/errors.md` are regenerated in the
sandbox by faithful extractors (`scripts/regen_plugin_compat_doc.py`,
`scripts/regen_errors_md.py`) that reproduce the generators' deterministic
output byte-for-byte from the source (`docs_gen.rs` consts / `errors.toml`);
the CI `docs-check` job is the final arbiter.
